<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ituzaingó</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1827</span> · Also known as Battle of Passo do Rosário · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ituzaingó, called Passo do Rosário in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, was fought on 20 February 1827 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul">Rio Grande do Sul</a> between the army of the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> under Carlos María de Alvear and the Brazilian imperial army under the Marquis of Barbacena. The Brazilians withdrew, but the victory was not decisive, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a> ended in 1828 with the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ituzaingo.jpg" alt="Battle of Ituzaingó" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Washt Rodrigues · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Infantaria_Brasileira_em_Passo_do_Ros%C3%A1rio.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
